.TH lx900e-app 1 "2026-10-30" "lx900e-cups 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lx900e-app \- PAPPL printer application for the Primera LX900e label printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lx900e-app
.RB [ \-\-device " uri" ]
.RB [ \-\-printer " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-port " port" ]
.RB [ \-\-spool " directory" ]
.RB [ \-\-log " file" ]
.RB [ \-\-state " file" ]
.RB [ \-\-no-state ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-check-device ]
.RB [ \-\-no-tls ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lx900e-app
is a PAPPL-based IPP Everywhere printer application for the Primera LX900e
colour label printer.
It exposes the printer without a PPD, so it can be used with CUPS 3,
AirPrint, Mopria, and other IPP Everywhere clients.
.PP
PWG raster jobs are accepted directly.
PDF and PostScript jobs are converted to CUPS raster with Ghostscript and
then passed to the same encoder as the CUPS 2 filter, so a page prints the
same way through either path.
.PP
The application advertises the 1200 dpi native resolution and the page sizes
from the PPD.  The common sizes are exposed as virtual roll sources, because
AirPrint and Mopria build their paper-size menu from the ready media of each
source; there is still only one physical roll.  The largest size is advertised
without a ready source because PAPPL allows at most 16 sources.
Ink levels and the media sensor are read from the printer's status block over
USB and reported as IPP supplies and state reasons.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " uri"
Create one printer for the given device URI, for example
.B usb://Primera/Color_Label_900?serial=00000001
or
.BR file:/tmp/capture.prn .
.TP
.BI \-\-printer " name"
Printer name for
.BR \-\-device .
Defaults to
.BR LX900e .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
IPP port, default 8000.
.TP
.BI \-\-spool " directory"
Spool directory.
The default is
.B /var/spool/lx900e-app
for root and
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/lx900e-app
for other users.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Log file, default standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " file"
State file, default
.B SPOOL/state.
.TP
.B \-\-no-state
Do not load or save printer state.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable PAPPL debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-check-device
Open the
.B \-\-device
URI, report success, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no-tls
Do not advertise or require IPPS/TLS.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.SH PRINT OPTIONS
.TP
.B lx900-ink-cartridge
Which cartridges are fitted:
.BR Color " (CMY only),"
.BR Black " (black only) or"
.BR ColorBlack " (both, the default)."
This is the same option as the CUPS 2 PPD's
.BR InkCartridge .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/lx900.conf
Registration offsets, shared with the CUPS 2 filter:
.PP
.nf
    # dots at 1200 dpi; left may be negative
    left=0
    top=4
.fi
.PP
The environment variables
.B LX900_LEFT_OFFSET
and
.B LX900_TOP_OFFSET
override the file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground against the printer and open the web interface:
.PP
.nf
    lx900e-app --device 'usb://Primera/Color_Label_900?serial=00000001' \\
        --printer LX900e --port 8000 \\
        --spool "$HOME/.local/state/lx900e-app"
.fi
.PP
Print a PDF through the application:
.PP
.nf
    ipptool -tv ipp://localhost:8000/ipp/print/LX900e print-job.test
.fi
.SH NOTES
The status query opens the USB device for a moment.
It is only made while the printer is idle, at most every ten seconds, and
never for
.B file:
or
.B socket:
devices.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lp (1),
.BR lpadmin (8),
.BR lx900-send (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jochen Schneider.
